VK, validation: a vertex attribute is bound to its stream's binding slot, and its stream must exist.

PipelineVK::Create sets VkVertexInputAttributeDescription::binding to attribute.streamIndex, while
the binding that stream describes is stream.bindingSlot; D3D12 goes through the stream (InputSlot =
stream.bindingSlot). With streams declared in slot order the two agree, which hides it. Since
42ddcff.

This reads the binding from the attribute's stream, as D3D12 does. Validation refuses an attribute
whose streamIndex is not below streamNum: nothing checked it, and both backends read
streams[streamIndex] past the array (D3D12 always did; the Vulkan fix makes it so there too).
Measured on v190, NVIDIA, Khronos layer on: a quad fed by two streams declared out of slot order
(streams[0] in slot 1 with stride 4, streams[1] in slot 0 with stride 8) drew nothing on Vulkan
(2,162 of 4,096 pixels wrong), with "VUID-vkCmdBindVertexBuffers2-pStrides-06209 ... The pStrides
value (4) ... is less than the extent of the binding for the attribute (8)"; D3D12 drew it exactly.
With the change both draw the image of the same quad from one interleaved stream, byte for byte, and
the layer is silent. An attribute with streamIndex 1 of one stream created a pipeline on both
backends; with the change it is refused with INVALID_ARGUMENT, naming streamIndex.

diff --git a/Source/VK/PipelineVK.hpp b/Source/VK/PipelineVK.hpp
index 7cd0017..d283392 100644
--- a/Source/VK/PipelineVK.hpp
+++ b/Source/VK/PipelineVK.hpp
@@ -164,7 +164,7 @@ Result PipelineVK::Create(const GraphicsPipelineDesc& graphicsPipelineDesc) {
             VkVertexInputAttributeDescription& vertexAttributeDesc = vertexAttributeDescs[i];
             vertexAttributeDesc = {};
             vertexAttributeDesc.location = attribute.vk.location;
-            vertexAttributeDesc.binding = attribute.streamIndex;
+            vertexAttributeDesc.binding = vi->streams[attribute.streamIndex].bindingSlot;
             vertexAttributeDesc.format = GetVkFormat(attribute.format);
             vertexAttributeDesc.offset = attribute.offset;
         }
